-- title:
--   Regularity of R/(x) for x ∈ 𝔪 ∖ 𝔪²
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a regular local ring, i.e. Noetherian local with the minimal number of generators of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `maximalIdeal R` equal to its Krull dimension. Let $x \in R$ satisfy three conditions: $x \in \mathfrak m$; $x \notin \mathfrak m^2$; and $x$ lies in no minimal prime of $R$, that is, $x \notin p$ for every $p \in$ `minimalPrimes R`. Assume moreover that the quotient ring $R/(x)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the single element $x$, is local. The conclusion is twofold: first, $R/(x)$ is again a regular local ring; second, the minimal number of generators of the maximal ideal of $R/(x)$, measured by `Submodule.spanFinrank`, is one less than that of $\mathfrak m$, stated in the form $\operatorname{spanFinrank}(\mathfrak m_{R/(x)}) + 1 = \operatorname{spanFinrank}(\mathfrak m)$. No assumption that $x$ is a non-zerodivisor is made; avoidance of the minimal primes is what replaces it.
--
--   This is the standard criterion for cutting down a regular local ring by one element: an element of $\mathfrak m \setminus \mathfrak m^2$ avoiding the minimal primes gives a regular quotient of embedding dimension, and hence dimension, one smaller. It serves as the inductive step in the proof that regular local rings are domains, and is used in the project in arguments about unramified extensions of Dedekind domains and in the local analysis of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_of_notMem_sq_of_forall_minimalPrimes_notMem.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
